  "contracts": [
    "Legacy default Text mode remains AND substring over title/body/tag/notebook text. Existing selectors remain independent AND restrictions.",
    "Explicit Filters mode supports text/title/body/tag/notebook/type/iscompleted clauses and implicit AND. Multiple positive notebook clauses form OR over matching base-title trees; negative notebook scopes exclude descendants.",
    "The standalone grammar preserves quoted field splitting, partial/unclosed quotes, known-filter colon handling, unknown-filter text fallback, type/completion validation and original wildcard term representation within 500 UTF-16 characters and 64 terms.",
    "Tag/notebook patterns preserve SQL LIKE percent/underscore semantics and original star-to-percent conversion; ASCII case folds, non-ASCII case does not. No query-controlled regular expressions are created.",
    "Text/title/body evaluation is literal case-insensitive substring matching, intentionally different from FTS tokenization, original normalization and relevance ranking. Free Filters text searches title/body only.",
    "Nonempty parsed any/date/resource/sourceurl/id/location clauses and text/title/body wildcard clauses fail explicitly. Dropped empty raw fields add no condition. Empty substring clauses match all corresponding text fields as an explicit local policy.",
    "Search performs no saved-state mutation, save, recovery replay, draft replacement, notebook operation or export. New query errors must preserve every persisted byte and unsaved field."
  ],
